```js
import { initializeApp } from "firebase/app";
import { getAI, getGenerativeModel, VertexAIBackend } from "firebase/ai";

const firebaseApp = initializeApp({
  // your Firebase config
});

// Use the Vertex AI Gemini API backend
const ai = getAI(firebaseApp, { backend: new VertexAIBackend() });

// Optionally specify a location (defaults to "us-central1")
// const ai = getAI(firebaseApp, { backend: new VertexAIBackend("europe-west4") });

const model = getGenerativeModel(ai, { model: "gemini-2.5-flash" });

const result = await model.generateContent("Write a haiku about Firebase.");
console.log(result.response.text());
```

The Vertex AI Gemini API requires your Firebase project to be on the Blaze (pay-as-you-go) plan. You also need to enable the Vertex AI API for the project, which you can do in the Firebase console under the AI Logic setup flow.

