In v9, features and row models are opt-in. Register the sorting feature and add a sorted row model:

```tsx
import {
  useTable,
  tableFeatures,
  rowSortingFeature,
  createSortedRowModel,
  sortFns,
  createColumnHelper,
  flexRender,
} from '@tanstack/react-table'

type Person = { name: string; age: number }

const _features = tableFeatures({ rowSortingFeature })
const columnHelper = createColumnHelper<typeof _features, Person>()

const columns = [
  columnHelper.accessor('name', { header: 'Name' }),
  columnHelper.accessor('age', { header: 'Age' }),
]

export function PeopleTable({ data }: { data: Person[] }) {
  const table = useTable({
    _features,
    _rowModels: {
      sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(sortFns),
    },
    columns,
    data,
  })

  return (
    <table>
      <thead>
        {table.getHeaderGroups().map(group => (
          <tr key={group.id}>
            {group.headers.map(header => (
              <th
                key={header.id}
                onClick={header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()}
                style={{ cursor: header.column.getCanSort() ? 'pointer' : undefined }}
              >
                {flexRender(header.column.columnDef.header, header.getContext())}
                {{ asc: ' ↑', desc: ' ↓' }[header.column.getIsSorted() as string] ?? null}
              </th>
            ))}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {table.getRowModel().rows.map(row => (
          <tr key={row.id}>
            {row.getVisibleCells().map(cell => (
              <td key={cell.id}>
                {flexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())}
              </td>
            ))}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  )
}
```

- `rowSortingFeature` adds the sorting state and column APIs (`getToggleSortingHandler`, `getIsSorted`, `getCanSort`).
- `createSortedRowModel(sortFns)` does the client-side sorting. Without it, nothing gets sorted.
- To disable sorting on a column, set `enableSorting: false` in its column def. To use a specific sort function, set `sortFn` (for example `'alphanumeric'`).

v9 is new and its API has changed during the pre-release cycle, so check the names above against the official docs for your exact version if anything doesn't resolve.

